Move walk state from dag/ to controller/ (#261)

## What

`dag/walkstate.go` defined `NodeState`, `PlanState`, `PlanSummary` —
reconcile-time outputs living in a compile-time package. `errors.go`,
`status.go`, and `foreach.go` imported `dag/` solely for these types.

## Changes

Move `walkstate.go` from `dag/` to `controller/`. Update all references.

## Result

`dag/` is now purely compile-time: one file (`dag.go`), three exported
types (`DAG`, `Topology`), three exported functions (`BuildDAG`,
`AssembleDAG`, `DetectCyclesEarly`). Zero reconcile-time concepts.

**Import cleanup:** `errors.go`, `status.go`, `foreach.go` no longer
import `dag/` at all. The remaining imports are for the actual DAG
struct.

The architecture is now legible from the import graph: `dag/` =
compile-time, `controller/` = reconcile-time.

## Verification

- `go build ./...` clean
- `go test -race ./controller/...` passes
- No behavioral changes — code move only
